# Quarantine for files this repository's working environment cannot delete
# (an `rm` inside the mounted working tree fails, so a file being removed is
# MOVED here instead). It was protected by .git/info/exclude alone, which is
# machine-local and does not travel with a clone — so on any other checkout
# the directory was untracked-but-visible and one `git add -A` away from being
# committed. Ignored here, where the ignore is part of the repository.
_to_delete/
